{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Evolutionary Software Architecture.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Evolutionary Software Architecture.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"evolutionary software architecture evolutionary software architecture","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Evolutionary Software Architecture.md","fileName":"Evolutionary Software Architecture.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Evolutionary Software Architecture","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 11:39\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Software Quality Attributes and Architecture Tradeoffs]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Software Quality Attributes and Architecture Tradeoffs","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Evolutionary Software Architecture.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Evolutionary Software Architecture.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"evolutionary software architecture evolutionary software architecture","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Evolutionary Software Architecture.md","fileName":"Evolutionary Software Architecture.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Evolutionary Software Architecture","heading":"Evolutionary Software Architecture","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Evolutionary software architecture preserves the ability to change a system safely as needs, load, and technology evolve. Modular boundaries, explicit contracts, tests, observability, and repeatable delivery make adaptation less dependent on risky system-wide rewrites.\n\nFuture change cannot be predicted in detail, so evolution is not permission to build speculative abstractions. The architecture should protect known change pressures and keep evidence available for revising decisions when the context changes.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Software Q